Casio Utilities - Installation

Linux
=====

Use the provided Makefile to compile and install the utilities:

make
make clean
sudo make install

This will compile the tape utilities into the src subdirectory and md100
into the md100 subdirectory and copy them together with the shell scripts
from the md100 subdirectory to /usr/local/bin.

Three shell scripts are provided to access MD100 floppies directly. Look at the
scripts and modify them to your needs.

fdutil-5.5 is needed for direct MD100 floppy disk access under Linux.
See md100/md100.txt for details.


Marcus von Cube
